Coverage reports count imported templates under separate compilation

When a program calls a template defined in another module, `-cov` now
records the hit in the defining module's listing even when the modules
are compiled separately. Previously the executed line could appear
unmarked or show zero hits, depending on which object the linker selected.

For example, save this template in `numbers.d`:
-------
module numbers;

int twice(T)(T x)
{
    return x + x;
}
-------

Save its caller in `sample.d`:
-------
module sample;
import numbers : twice;

unittest
{
    assert(twice(3) == 6);
}

void main() {}
-------

In a POSIX shell, compile the modules separately, link them, and run the test:

```console
dmd -unittest -cov -c numbers.d
dmd -unittest -cov -c sample.d
dmd -of=sample sample.o numbers.o
./sample
```

The test in `sample.d` passes with or without the fix. The difference is
visible in `numbers.lst`: previously the count beside `return x + x;` was
blank. Although the template is defined in `numbers.d`, its only caller is
in `sample.d`, so DMD emits `twice!int` in `sample.o`. That copy now records
its hit against the defining source line. After one execution, the listing
contains:

```console
      1|    return x + x;
```
